<title>USA: CITGO Petroleum unit to buy Sun terminal.</title>
<headline>CITGO Petroleum unit to buy Sun terminal.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE BELL, Pa. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petroleos de Venezuela SA subsidiary CITGO Petroleum Corp's CITGO Asphalt Refining Co unit said Thursday it entered into an agreement to buy Sun Co Inc's Cockpit, Va., asphalt terminal for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>Sun said earlier in the year it was exiting the asphalt business. CITGO said it expected to close the deal before the end of the year.</p>
<p>The terminal, located on the Potomac River 20 miles southwest of Washington D.C., has 12 asphalt storage tanks with capacity of about 85,000 barrels.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
